  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "2 v 2 – press and cover",
  "description": "Mark out an area of about 40 × 30 metres with cones, ideally across the rink with the boards as one side. Blue line up in two lines at one end and red in two lines at the other. The first blue passes to their partner and they attack 2 v 2. Blue score by skating with the ball over red's line. The first two red players skate out and try to win the ball: one presses and one covers.\n\nWhen red win the ball the attack is over, and the next attack starts from red going the other way with new players. If the ball goes over the boards, the team that did not touch it last gets a stroke-in.\n\nBuild it up: play towards two small goals at each end, or towards full-size goals with keepers who start the attacks with a throw. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The nearest defender presses the ball carrier – skate in close, but slow down so you are not skated past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The other sits at an angle behind, covering the space behind and ready to cut out the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Swap jobs as soon as the ball is passed: the cover becomes the presser."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Talk to each other – \"I've got him!\" and \"I'm covering!\"."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
